   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Origin and languages",
     "texto": [
      "To ask where someone is from, say «Waar kom je vandaan?». Notice that «vandaan» goes at the end. To answer: «Ik kom uit...» (I come from... / I'm from...). To ask about languages: «Spreek je Nederlands?» (Do you speak Dutch?). In questions, when «je» comes after the verb, the verb loses its final -t: «spreek je» (and not «spreekt je»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    }
   ]
  },
